It should move to directory /pub/Linux/devel/lang/c soon.

Here are some excerpts from README:

    This is version 1.1 of mph, an order preserving minimal perfect hash
    function generator for string keys. It uses the algorithm presented
    in the paper:

            A Family of Perfect Hashing Methods
            B. S. Majewski, N. C. Wormald, G. Havas and Z. J. Czech
            Computer Journal (to appear).

    The algorithm is probabilistic and runs fast in practice.

Here is a summary of changes from previous versions:

    1.1
        - mphminm: created. Finds the minimum constant that can be specified
          with mph's -m option. Useful for small keysets only.

        - mphm.c: created. Used by mphminm.

        - arb/keys.c:keynew(): bug fix - "kp->vals" was not being properly
          initialized. Thanks to Felix von Leitner <leitner@math.fu-berlin.de>
          for finding this bug.

