-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hi, Gals and Guys,

The Linux C library 5.4.13 is a bug-fixing release for libc 5.4.7.
There are no new features in this release. If there is new serious
bug report, the next public release of the Linux C library will be
6.0. The main features in libc 6.0, aka glibc 2.0, are MT-safe and
pthread support. With libc 6.0, Linux will enter an era of SMP kernel
support as well as the kernel-based pthread support. I have been
running an alpha version of libc 6.0 with gcc, binutils, bin86 and
XFree86 3.2. Everything looks very encouraging. I expect libc 6.0
will be released RSN.

If you use linux 2.1.x, you need libc 5.4.13 or above to compile libc
yourself. The pre-compiled libc should run fine under linux 2.1.x.
Also this library is compiled with -D_REENTRANT so that errno is MT
safe.

The shared libraries are now compiled with -g1 which can provide
minimum information when core dump happens. You can strip
libc.so.5.4.13 if you want.

Due to the new, improved locale, the Linux C library 5.4.13 is binary
compatible with libc 5.3.12 but not vice versa. The binaries
compiled/linked with libc.so.5.4.13 may not run with libc.so.5.3.12.
You may need to regenerate locale files for the new locale in libc
5.4.13 if you use locales other tha C/POSIX which are the defaults.

This is the public release of the Linux C library 5.4.13. Please read
the ChangeLog for details regarding changes/bug fixes.

DISTRIBUTION SITES:

The primary FTP sites for the compiler/C library are:

*     ftp://tsx-11.mit.edu/pub/linux/packages/GCC
*     ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/GCC

DISTRIBUTION FILES:

1.	libc-5.4.13.bin.tar.gz

REQUIRED. This package contains the header files for libc, shared and
static ELF libraries libc and libm, and the static ELF library libbsd.a. 
The header files in libc-5.4.13.bin.tar.gz are not complete. You need to
install the kernel source tree for the system-dependent header files.

The header files are in lib-x.y.z.bin.tar.gz and libc-x.y.z.tar.gz. You
can do

# gzip -dc lib-x.y.z.bin.tar.gz | tar xvvf - usr/include

to extract the header files without the binaries files. A separate
tar file for the header files may cause unnecessary confusion.

2.	libc-5.4.13.tar.gz
 
Source tree for libc and header files.

3.	libc-5.4.7-5.4.13.diff.gz

Context diffs against the source tree from the previous libc release.
Please make sure the empty libc/regex/rx.h is deleted.


H.J.
hjl@gnu.ai.mit.edu
11/22/96

