-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

rlpr 1.40 is now available.  although this release is mainly to fix
some portability issues to other unices, there are some other
enhancements.  among them:

   * behavior which mimics traditional berkeley `lpr' when rlpr is
     invoked as `lpr'
   * improved debugging support for getting your configuration
     to work properly
   * checks against arguments that could overflow poorly coded 
     lpd's are now enforced
   * long overdue seteuid()/setreuid() support

you are welcome to upgrade if you so desire.

Briefly, rlpr uses TCP/IP to send print jobs to lpd servers anywhere
on a network.  Unlike lpr, it *does not* require that the remote
printers be explicitly known to the machine you wish to print from,
(e.g. through /etc/printcap) and thus is considerably more flexible
and requires less administration.

Most importantly, one can use rlpr to print from a machine one does
not have root access on to a machine one does.  (no, this isn't a
security hole).  There are also some additinal configurations which
are possible -- please read rlpr's README for details.

rlpr can be obtained from the following sources:

    Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/system/Printing
		    65kB rlpr-1.40.tar.gz
    Alternate-site: sherilyn.wustl.edu /pub/

have fun,
meem

