Hello "Linux-Quakers",

This is the announcement for lxQuakeCDmusic 1.0, a set of scripts and
binaries which adds level-specific music to the Linux port of id's
popular game Quake. Just as with the original DOS version, you can now
assign arbitrary CD audio tracks to certain levels. While playing a
level, the appropriate track is auto-repeated, and hitting the "Pause"
key stops/resumes both, the game and the music server. You can have as
many files containing track-to-level assignments as you want to, and
easily activate them prior to starting x[f86]quake.

It was developed and tested on Linux/x86 (ELF, xquake 1.01 and 1.06),
but chances are that it also works for the Linux/Alpha port; see the
file bin/README for details. This file also contains comprehensive
installation and copyright notes, so it's really a good idea to have
a look at it... ;)

