Announcing the Multitrack-recorder for Linux!

This is the first beta-release of multitrack, a four-track
recorder for Linux. This program uses the harddisk for recording
of sound and SVGA-lib for displaying the interface. Since all
recorded tracks will be directly stored on harddisk there's
no limit to the length of each track (only the amount of
free harddisk space is important). It is possible to record
and playback at the same time if you have two wavedevices
(for example two audiocards). The program has a user friendly
interface for manipulation and playback of the recorded tracks. A
full-featured mixer is included.

Check out the following URL for more info

	http://rulhmpc38.leidenuniv.nl/private/multitrack/multitrack.html

The binary is obtainable via anonymous ftp:

	ftp://rulhmpc38.leidenuniv.nl/pub/multitrack/multitrack.tgz

Here's the Linux Projects Map entry...

