-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Etherboot-2.1 is a package containing code that can be put in a NIC
PROM to boot Linux diskless using bootp, tftp and/or NFS.

The major changes from 2.0 are that the 32 bit version fits in 8kbytes
so older cards with only room for a 2764 EPROM can be used; another new
version of mknbi, the same one used in netboot-0.3; some contributed
experimental patches for NFS swap for 2.0.x kernels, and a serial
console; and the usual round of quality improvements.

It has been uploaded into ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/Linux/Incoming and
should show up at mirrors everywhere soon, normally in the
system/Linux-boot directory. In the meantime it is also available from
ftp://ftp.syd.dit.csiro.au/pub/ken/etherboot-2.1.{tar.gz,lsm}.

	Ken

