Hello!

What is Turbo Vision
- --------------------
Turbo Vision is a library that provides an application framework.  With
TV you can write a beautiful object-oriented character-mode user interface
in short time.

TV is available in C++ and Pascal and is a product of Borland International.
It was developed to run on MS-DOS systems but today it is available for many
other platforms (ported by independent programmers).

This is the last version of my C++ port.  It is based on the Borland 2.0
version with fixes.

Main changes from release 0.1 to 0.2
- ------------------------------------
1. This release uses (n)curses functions to read keys and do video
   output (if the /dev/vcs* system can not be used).

2. The library now works well under X.  Keys are handled correctly.
   A monochrome palette is used.  Bold and inverse attributes are
   used to draw the text.  SIGWINCH signal is hooked so we can resize
   the screen at runtime.

3. Help system fixed.

4. Desktop save/Desktop load functions fixed.

Where download the library
- --------------------------
I uploaded the package to sunsite.unc.edu in directory /pub/Linux/Incoming.
The file will be moved to /pub/Linux/devel/lang/c++ in some days.  His name
is tv-0.2.tar.gz.

gpm and (n)curses libraries are required.

