DCF77 radio clock information for LINUX
=======================================

'dcf77time' reads from a DCF77-Module ('Atom Clock') via a serial
port the raw time transmitted at 77.5 Khz from a antenna located at
Mainflingen near Frankfurt/Main (Germany).  It is not that accurate
and doesn't provide date information, but it's very cheap (18 DM).

'dcf77time' is primary for use in Germany since it relies on the
DCF77 signal.  But it might be of interest to some surrounding
countries too.

Christian (chb@muc.de)

