With over forty members, the Akron Linux Users Group is a support group
for both the novice and the advanced user.  Topics of discussion range
from installations & upgrades, to network administration (DNS, NIS, NFS,
remote printers, network security issues, PPP/SLIP), as well as hardware
compatibility issues, internet connectivity, setting up X-windows, and a
plethora of other subjects every Linux operator ought to know.

Topics for next week's meeting:  

1) Redhat 4.0 vs. Slackware '96 - which is better?
   Despite the new and improved installation sequence developed by RedHat,
   some of our users were displeased with the final RedHat 4.0 product.
   Slackware '96 offers a better installation process than Slackware 3.0
   did, and the new Slackware looks nice.

2) Motif for Linux (Moo-tiff by Lasermoon & InfoMagic)
   So what can be done with the Motif Window Manager?  Is it speedier than
   fvwm/95 or twm?  What about Motif application development?  We'll have
   a machine with Motif loaded on it to demo if anyone is interested.

3) Setting up a listserver...
   There are a couple of people in the Akron Linux User's Group who are
   interested in setting up a listserver.  The Majordomo listserver
   installation / configuration will be discussed.

        See you at the meeting!
        -Chris Cole
         cole@lynkmedia.com

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

The meeting place is at "Coffee Configurations", which is a cyber-cafe on
Exchange Street, just east of Brown Street in Akron.  The meeting dates
are every second and fourth Wednesday at 8:00pm.

