- ---------------------------------------------

JAZZ - a free midi sequencer for Linux and MS-Windows

JAZZ is a full size midi sequencer allowing record/play and many
edit functions as quantize, copy, transpose ..., multiple undo;
two main windows operating on whole tracks and single events;
graphic pitch editing, GS sound editing functions and much more ...

JAZZ is copyright (C) by Andreas Voss and Per Sigmond, and is
distributed under the terms of the GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE
(Gnu GPL). 

We are happy to announce that JAZZ version 2.6 is ready for download.
Both MS-Windows and Linux/Un*x versions as well as source code is 
available.

News in version 2.6: 
- - Improved file handling 
- - Load/save of patterns (e.g. a drum groove) 
- - Save current window geometry 
- - Pianowin closeable (not displayed until bar selected from trackwin) 
- - Example added on use of random rhythm generator and harmony browser 
- - Documentation updates 
- - Improvements to random rhythm generator: 
  - Save/load settings 
- - Improvements to harmony browser: 
  - Save/load settings 
  - Toolbar 
  - Analyze harmonies 
  - Harmonies can be displayed in pianowin 


