I released mv1000drv-0.24, the newest version of the driver and library
for the MuTech MV-1000 PCI-framegrabber.
This driver is not supported by MuTech.
It is available on ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/apps/video/
(currently in the Incoming dir)
The documentation for many chips used by the MV-1000 is
available on: 
ftp://wpfd25.physik.uni-wuerzburg.de /pub/linux/fgrabber/mv1000
or on Linux-LAB mirrors.

features:

- - master transfer: 
	30 MB/s on i82437 
	55 MB/s on i82439

- - slave transfer ( 1-4MB onboard memory )

- - free programable PLL-synthesizer is able to regenerate 
  pixelclock (3-40MHz) from hsync (5-64kHz).

- - free programable grabwindow.
 

New in this release:

- - Tk-Extension which allows external processes to draw to a Tk-window,
  used for displaying the videoimage from Tcl/Tk.

- - Camera configuration programm working with rs170 config files

- - New library functions for finding a private colormap which
  is very similar to the default colormap. 

- - alpha documentation in postscript format.


Requirements: 

- - Linux Kernel 2.0 
- - gcc-2.7.2, libc.so.5.0.9 or later ( C++ comments are used, and
  I don't know how to use them with gcc-2.7.0) 
- - libtk.so.4 and libtcl.so7.4 for the Tcl-configuration programm. 
- - modules-1.2.8.tgz or newer (insmod, rmmod .. ) 
- - libjpeg.so.6 (don't forget the include files)
- - X11R6, XFree-3.1.2 
- - flex

Copying-policy:    GPL

For mor information see:

	http://wpfd25.physik.uni-wuerzburg.de/~karrer/mv1000/mv1000.html


