-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

BSPlib is a parallel programming library based on the 
Bulk Synchronous Parallel (BSP) programming model.
For more information on BSP see http://www.bsp-worldwide.org

BSPlib is implemented and distributed under the name of  
the Oxford BSP Toolset and Profiling system (v0.6beta).

It consists of:

1) A library of BSP (Bulk Synchronous Parallel) communication and
   synchronisation primitives using either Bulk Synchronous Message
   Passing (BSMP) or Direct Remote Memory Access (DRMA), callable
   from Fortran, C++ and C code.

2) A performance profiling tool for performance prediction of
   BSP application code.

3) Manual pages for the BSPlib function calls.

Sources and binaries (in tar.gz format) of Oxford BSP 
Toolset and Profiling system (v0.6beta) are available at:

http://www.bsp-worldwide.org/implmnts/tool06b.htm

Source and binary RPMs of the Oxford BSP Toolset and 
Profiling system (v0.6beta) for Linux are available at:

http://pegasus.cc.ucf.edu/~dsd75511

