ivtools-0.5.tar.gz" "get ivtools ivmaps-0.5.tar.gz" as the body of a
message (no subject required) to listproc@viewport.com.

ivtools is a C++ framework for constructing custom drawing editors.
It incorporates backward-compatible copies of InterViews 3.1 and the
Unidraw library from the last tar file published by Mark Linton
(3.2a.tar.Z).  It extends John Vlissides' Unidraw with:

	- double-buffered graphics
	- improved pan/zoom of large images
	- script save/restore of graphic objects 
	- attributes (property lists) for graphic objects
	- multi-frame editor/viewer
	- node-and-edge graph editor/viewer

It also provides a user interface to the clippoly package:
http://www.ph.tn.tudelft.nl/People/klamer/clippoly_entry.html

ivmaps is a C++ framework for map viewers (2D and 3D) derived from
ivtools.  It supports VPF and DLG vector map formats as well as 1
degree DEM from the USGS.  It utilizes PROJ-4.3 (cartographic
projection) and vtk1.2 (3d Open GL visualization).

